rmal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>Now we=E2=80=
=99re witnessing protests by young people in France, who share the anger of=
 other Gen Z around the world, but not the same political power. Because un=
like their contemporaries outside the West, young people in Europe are a sh=
rinking demographic. Today my colleague Amanda Taub writes about the genera=
tional tensions in the West=E2=80=99s aging societies and why they risk bec=
oming a vicious cycle.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,=
